# Project 3, U-Boot: THE MARKER ONLY.
#
# This is what the BASELINE is built with. It adds the first electrical
# marker to Project 2's configuration and changes nothing else, so that
# the baseline measures Project 2's boot rather than an already improved
# one.
#
# The trimming lives in fast.config, which is the 10-uboot variant. Two
# files rather than one file with lines commented in and out: that dance
# was the original design, it is invisible in a diff, and the instruction
# describing it was wrong within a day of being written. One change, one
# fragment, one result directory, as everywhere else in this project.

# The preboot command runs before the boot delay and before any storage
# scanned, which is what makes D1 the start of the measured interval
# rather than a point somewhere inside U-Boot.
#
# CLEAR BEFORE SET, AND THE CLEAR IS NOT REDUNDANT. PG11 has no pull
# resistor: driven high and released it reads 1, driven low and released
# it reads 0, measured at the U-Boot prompt on Monday 21 September 2026.
# It holds whatever it was last driven to.
#
# Nothing in the Linux device tree claims the pin, so it is still high
# from the previous run when the next capture begins two seconds later.
# A bare "gpio set" then drives high a line that is already high and
# there is no edge for anything to find. Six baseline runs recorded D1
# high in all 1.6 million samples with zero transitions, and analyze.py
# discarded every one of them saying U-Boot never started.
#
# The clear pulls the line down, the set raises it microseconds later,
# and the rising edge exists regardless of where the line was sitting.
CONFIG_USE_PREBOOT=y
CONFIG_PREBOOT="gpio clear PG11; gpio set PG11"

# Without this, "gpio" is not a command U-Boot has, the preboot names
# something that does not exist, and the failure is silent as far as the
# trace is concerned: the board boots normally and D1 never moves.
CONFIG_CMD_GPIO=y
